ol_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"2b54dca0-4775-4427-9d07-b37612b7752d\",\"uuid\":\"5d218512-0991-44a7-9840-494c0e69b6e2\",\"error\":\"unknown\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_orig_mnqwy3c7hfqtgzdfmqztqzrxgi2danrsg5qwmzrxgq3tqmy\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Beam Splitter\\n2\\t\\n3\\tBuild a beam propagation simulator for a 2D grid laboratory.\\n4\\t\\n5\\t## Grid Format\\n6\\t\\n7\\tThe grid is a 2D array of single-character strings:\\n8\\t\\n9\\t- `'S'` — beam source (always on the top row). Emits a beam straight down.\\n10\\t- `'^'` — splitter. When a beam arrives, it splits into two diagonal beams.\\n11\\t- `'.'` — empty cell. Beams pass through.\\n12\\t\\n13\\tBeams that leave the grid boundaries are absorbed (they stop).\\n14\\t\\n15\\t## Beam Movement Rules\\n16\\t\\n17\\t1. A beam from the source `'S'` moves **straight down** (row+1, same column) each step.\\n18\\t2. When a beam hits a splitter `'^'`, it splits into **two beams**:\\n19\\t   - One goes **down-left** (row+1, col-1)\\n20\\t   - One goes **down-right** (row+1, col+1)\\n21\\t   The original beam is consumed by the splitter (it does not continue straight).\\n22\\t3. An unsplit beam (not at a splitter) continues in its current direction:\\n23\\t   - A downward beam continues downward (row+1, same col)\\n24\\t   - A down-left beam continues down-left (row+1, col-1)\\n25\\t   - A down-right beam continues down-right (row+1, col+1)\\n26\\t4. A beam is **absorbed** when it moves outside the grid boundaries (row < 0, row >= rows, col < 0, col >= cols).\\n27\\t5. Multiple beams can occupy the same cell simultaneously.\\n28\\t6. Splitters always split regardless of the beam's incoming direction.\\n29\\t\\n30\\t## API\\n31\\t\\n32\\tExport two functions from `src/index.ts`:\\n33\\t\\n34\\t### `countBeamCells(grid: string[][]): number`\\n35\\t\\n36\\tCount the number of distinct cells visited by any beam. A cell counts once even if multiple beams pass through it. The source cell `'S'` counts as visited. Splitter cells hit by beams count as visited.\\n37\\t\\n38\\t### `countBeamPaths(grid: string[][]): bigint`\\n39\\t\\n40\\tCount the total number of distinct source-to-exit paths through the grid. Each time a beam splits at `'^'`, both branches are separate paths. A path ends when the beam exits the grid (moves beyond any edge).\\n41\\t\\n42\\tWith K splitters along a beam's path, there are potentially 2^K paths. The result can be astronomically large, so return a `bigint`.\\n43\\t\\n44\\t**Performance constraint**: Must handle a 200x200 grid with up to 50 splitters and return results in under 5 seconds. Enumerating individual paths is not feasible for large inputs.\\n45\\t\\n46\\t## Example\\n47\\t\\n48\\t```\\n49\\tGrid (4 rows x 5 cols):\\n50\\t. S . . .\\n51\\t. . . . .\\n52\\t. ^ . . .\\n53\\t. . . . .\\n54\\t```\\n55\\t\\n56\\t- The beam starts at (0,1) where `'S'` is.\\n57\\t- It moves down: (1,1), (2,1) — hits splitter.\\n58\\t- Splits into down-left (3,0) and down-right (3,2).\\n59\\t- Both beams exit the grid after row 3.\\n60\\t- Visited cells: (0,1), (1,1), (2,1), (3,0), (3,2) → `countBeamCells` returns **5**.\\n61\\t- Paths: 2 distinct paths (one ending at (3,0), one at (3,2)) → `countBeamPaths` returns **2n**.\\n62\\t\\n63\\t```\\n64\\tGrid with two splitters:\\n65\\t. S . . .\\n66\\t. ^ . . .\\n67\\t^ . ^ . .\\n68\\t. . . . .\\n69\\t```\\n70\\t\\n71\\t- Beam starts at (0,1), moves to (1,1) — hits splitter.\\n72\\t- Splits: down-left to (2,0) hits another splitter, down-right to (2,2) hits another splitter.\\n73\\t- (2,0) splitter: sends beams to (3,-1) absorbed and (3,1).\\n74\\t- (2,2) splitter: sends beams to (3,1) and (3,3).\\n75\\t- `countBeamCells`: (0,1), (1,1), (2,0), (2,2), (3,1), (3,3) → **6** (note: two beams land on (3,1) but it counts once).\\n76\\t- `countBeamPaths`: 4 paths total, but one is absorbed → **3n** paths that exit through the bottom or sides at valid cells... Actually, all 4 paths exit (absorbed = exits grid): paths to (3,-1), (3,1), (3,1), (3,3) → **4n**.\\n77\\t\\n78\\t## Commands\\n79\\t\\n80\\t```bash\\n81\\tnpm test        # run tests\\n82\\tnpm run build   # compile TypeScript\\n83\\tnpm run lint    # lint source\\n84\\t```\\n85\\t\\n86\\t## File Structure\\n87\\t\\n88\\tPlace your implementation in `src/`. The main entry point should be `src/index.ts`.\\n89\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"2b54dca0-4775-4427-9d07-b37612b7752d\",\"uuid\":\"b575e267-3ff0-4184-8b55-3ac7045aab76\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-18T04:15:50.946Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/TASK.md\",\"content\":\"# Beam Splitter\\n\\nBuild a beam propagation simulator for a 2D grid laboratory.\\n\\n## Grid Format\\n\\nThe grid is a 2D array of single-character strings:\\n\\n- `'S'` — beam source (always on the top row). Emits a beam straight down.\\n- `'^'` — splitter. When a beam arrives, it splits into two diagonal beams.\\n- `'.'` — empty cell. Beams pass through.\\n\\nBeams that leave the grid boundaries are absorbed (they stop).\\n\\n## Beam Movement Rules\\n\\n1. A beam from the source `'S'` moves **straight down** (row+1, same column) each step.\\n2. When a beam hits a splitter `'^'`, it splits into **two beams**:\\n   - One goes **down-left** (row+1, col-1)\\n   - One goes **down-right** (row+1, col+1)\\n   The original beam is consumed by the splitter (it does not continue straight).\\n3. An unsplit beam (not at a splitter) continues in its current direction:\\n   - A downward beam continues downward (row+1, same col)\\n   - A down-left beam continues down-left (row+1, col-1)\\n   - A down-right beam continues down-right (row+1, col+1)\\n4. A beam is **absorbed** when it moves outside the grid boundaries (row < 0, row >= rows, col < 0, col >= cols).\\n5. Multiple beams can occupy the same cell simultaneously.\\n6. Splitters always split regardless of the beam's incoming direction.\\n\\n## API\\n\\nExport two functions from `src/index.ts`:\\n\\n### `countBeamCells(grid: string[][]): number`\\n\\nCount the number of distinct cells visited by any beam. A cell counts once even if multiple beams pass through it. The source cell `'S'` counts as visited. Splitter cells hit by beams count as visited.\\n\\n### `countBeamPaths(grid: string[][]): bigint`\\n\\nCount the total number of distinct source-to-exit paths through the grid. Each time a beam splits at `'^'`, both branches are separate paths. A path ends when the beam exits the grid (moves beyond any edge).\\n\\nWith K splitters along a beam's path, there are potentially 2^K paths. The result can be astronomically large, so return a `bigint`.\\n\\n**Performance constraint**: Must handle a 200x200 grid with up to 50 splitters and return results in under 5 seconds. Enumerating individual paths is not feasible for large inputs.\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n```\\nGrid (4 rows x 5 cols):\\n. S . . .\\n. . . . .\\n. ^ . . .\\n. . . . .\\n```\\n\\n- The beam starts at (0,1) where `'S'` is.\\n- It moves down: (1,1), (2,1) — hits splitter.\\n- Splits into down-left (3,0) and down-right (3,2).\\n- Both beams exit the grid after row 3.\\n- Visited cells: (0,1), (1,1), (2,1), (3,0), (3,2) → `countBeamCells` returns **5**.\\n- Paths: 2 distinct paths (one ending at (3,0), one at (3,2)) → `countBeamPaths` returns **2n**.\\n\\n```\\nGrid with two splitters:\\n. S . . .\\n. ^ . . .\\n^ . ^ . .\\n. . . . .\\n```\\n\\n- Beam starts at (0,1), moves to (1,1) — hits splitter.\\n- Splits: down-left to (2,0) hits another splitter, down-right to (2,2) hits another splitter.\\n- (2,0) splitter: sends beams to (3,-1) absorbed and (3,1).\\n- (2,2) splitter: sends beams to (3,1) and (3,3).\\n- `countBeamCells`: (0,1), (1,1), (2,0), (2,2), (3,1), (3,3) → **6** (note: two beams land on (3,1) but it counts once).\\n- `countBeamPaths`: 4 paths total, but one is absorbed → **3n** paths that exit through the bottom or sides at valid cells... Actually, all 4 paths exit (absorbed = exits grid): paths to (3,-1), (3,1), (3,1), (3,3) → **4n**.\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm test        # run tests\\nnpm run build   # compile TypeScript\\nnpm run lint    # lint source\\n```\\n\\n## File Structure\\n\\nPlace your implementation in `src/`. The main entry point should be `src/index.ts`.\\n\",\"numLines\":89,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":89}}}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_orig_mnqwy3c7gezdcnbtme2wimjzmezdeoldgfrgimbrmeywcnq\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t{\\n2\\t  \\\"name\\\": \\\"bench-beam-splitter\\\",\\n3\\t  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n4\\t  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Beam splitter reasoning benchmark\\\",\\n5\\t  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n6\\t  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n7\\t    \\\"build\\\": \\\"tsc\\\",\\n8\\t    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"eslint src/\\\",\\n9\\t    \\\"test\\\": \\\"vitest run\\\"\\n10\\t  },\\n11\\t  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n12\\t    \\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"^25.2.3\\\",\\n13\\t    \\\"@typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin\\\": \\\"^7.0.0\\\",\\n14\\t    \\\"@typescript-eslint/parser\\\": \\\"^7.0.0\\\",\\n15\\t    \\\"eslint\\\": \\\"^8.56.0\\\",\\n16\\t    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"^5.4.0\\\",\\n17\\t    \\\"@vitest/coverage-v8\\\": \\\"^2.0.0\\\",\\n18\\t    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"^2.0.0\\\"\\n19\\t  }\\n20\\t}\\n21\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"2b54dca0-4775-4427-9d07-b37612b7752d\",\"uuid\":\"57824ca2-7b2c-4f98-ab9a-1a2cb10c78a9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-18T04:15:50.946Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/package.json\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"bench-beam-splitter\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Beam splitter reasoning benchmark\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"tsc\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"eslint src/\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"vi